{c: Chords from the writer's own lead sheet (MusicXML in the source above)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm]My heart is [Ebmaj7]sure, O God.
[Gm]I am se[Ebmaj7]cure, O God.
[Bb]With [Gm]every[Ebmaj7]thing [Bb]my soul will [F]sing to You.
[Gm]I will a[Ebmaj7]waken the dawn.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Eb]Great are you, Lord; [Bb]higher than heavens.
[Fsus4]Your faithfulness [Eb]fills the skies.
Be ex[Eb]alted, O Lord, a[Bb]bove all the heavens
[Fsus4]And let Your glory rise!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]You are a [Ebmaj7]given, O God.
[Gm]You will de[Ebmaj7]liver, O God.
[Bb]Sal[Gm]vation You [Ebmaj7]bring, so [Bb]my soul will [F]sing to You.
[Gm]I will a[Ebmaj7]waken the dawn.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Eb]I [F/Eb]will [Bb]sing to You.
[F]I will [Gm7]sing to You.
[Eb]I will [Bb]praise You, O God, [F]before the world!
{end_of_bridge}
